.Dd August 2, 2026
.Dt ZWC 1
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm zwc
.Nd word, line, character, and byte count for compressed files
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl -libxo
.Op Fl c | Fl m
.Op Fl Llw
.Op Ar file ...
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The
.Nm
utility is a thin front-end to
.Xr wc 1
that decompresses known compressed inputs before counting.
It is especially useful for
.Fx
man pages and other compressed text, where a direct
.Xr wc 1
invocation would report statistics for the compressed byte stream
rather than the underlying document.
.Pp
Each
.Ar file
argument is classified by suffix and decompressed to a pipe into
.Xr wc 1
as follows:
.Bl -column ".Pa .zst / .zstd" ".Xr zstdcat 1" -offset indent
.It Sy Suffix Ta Sy Decompressor
.It Pa .Z , .gz Ta Xr zcat 1
.It Pa .bz2 Ta Xr bzcat 1
.It Pa .lzma Ta Xr lzcat 1
.It Pa .xz Ta Xr xzcat 1
.It Pa .zst , .zstd Ta Xr zstdcat 1
.El
.Pp
All other files are passed to
.Xr wc 1
unchanged.
Options are forwarded to
.Xr wc 1 .
.Pp
The following options are available:
.Bl -tag -width "--libxo"
.It Fl -libxo
Generate output via
.Xr libxo 3
in a selection of different human and machine readable formats.
See
.Xr xo_options 7
for details on command line arguments.
.It Fl L
Write the length of the longest line.
.It Fl c
Write the number of bytes.
.It Fl l
Write the number of lines.
.It Fl m
Write the number of characters.
.It Fl w
Write the number of words.
.El
.Pp
When an option is specified,
.Nm
only reports the information requested by that option.
The default action matches
.Xr wc 1
.Pq lines, words, and bytes .
See
.Xr wc 1
for precise definitions of lines, words, bytes, and characters.
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Ex -std
.Pp
Like
.Xr wc 1 ,
.Nm
continues processing remaining
.Ar file
arguments after an error and reports failure only when exiting.
.Sh EXAMPLES
Count lines in a compressed man page:
.Pp
.Dl "zwc -l /usr/share/man/man1/wc.1.gz"
.Pp
Find the longest line across several compressed manuals:
.Pp
.Dl "zwc -L /usr/share/man/man1/*.1.gz"
.Pp
Mix compressed and plain inputs:
.Pp
.Dl "zwc -w README.md NOTES.gz archive.xz"
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr bzcat 1 ,
.Xr gzip 1 ,
.Xr lzcat 1 ,
.Xr wc 1 ,
.Xr xzcat 1 ,
.Xr zcat 1 ,
.Xr zstdcat 1 ,
.Xr libxo 3 ,
.Xr xo_options 7
.Sh HISTORY
The
.Nm
utility appeared in FrauBSD.
